  "name": "rosetta-fibonacci-sequence",
  "snippet": false,
  "code": "use IO.Std.write_line;\nuse Ghul.Pipes.Pipe;\n\n// A generator: each `yield` hands the consumer the next element and suspends, so the sequence is\n// unbounded and only as much of it is computed as the consumer asks for.\nfibonacci() -> Pipe[long] is\n    let current mut = 0L;\n    let next mut = 1L;\n\n    while true do\n        yield current;\n\n        let following = current + next;\n        current = next;\n        next = following;\n    od\nsi\n\nfor f in fibonacci() | .take(10) do\n    write_line(\"{f}\");\nod",
  "fullSource": "use IO.Std.write_line;\nuse Ghul.Pipes.Pipe;\n\n// A generator: each `yield` hands the consumer the next element and suspends, so the sequence is\n// unbounded and only as much of it is computed as the consumer asks for.\nfibonacci() -> Pipe[long] is\n    let current mut = 0L;\n    let next mut = 1L;\n\n    while true do\n        yield current;\n\n        let following = current + next;\n        current = next;\n        next = following;\n    od\nsi\n\nfor f in fibonacci() | .take(10) do\n    write_line(\"{f}\");\nod\n",
